      "rationale": "The story map produced 26 distinct clusters from 433 results. The dominant story (38 sources) — FM Faisal's intensive diplomatic consultation blitz — confirms and deepens the escalating alignment posture. But the week also generated four analytically significant new developments not reducible to last week's frame: (1) Zelenskyy's second Saudi visit in weeks, producing a formal 'strategic security arrangement' across air defense, energy, and food security — a genuinely new bilateral dimension; (2) India NSA Doval visiting Riyadh on PM Modi's explicit instructions, confirming Saudi Arabia as an essential energy-security interlocutor for a major non-Western power; (3) Saudi Aramco in reported talks to purchase Ukrainian interceptor drones to defend oil fields from confirmed Iranian strikes, representing an escalation from passive defense to active counter-measure procurement; and (4) Saudi Arabia blocking a $1.5 billion Pakistan-Sudan arms deal, demonstrating offensive-adjacent security statecraft previously not formally tracked. Four stories with 5+ sources did not generate significant movement assessments: Story #9 (Newcastle United, 10 sources) is PIF sports portfolio continuation with no posture change signal; Story #17 (Filipino twins surgery, 6 sources) is KSrelief soft power routine; Story #18 (KSrelief distributions, 6 sources) is humanitarian diplomacy continuation; Story #21 (Al-Ahli AFC, 3 sources) is domestic regime routine. Coverage volumes on these are noted but do not alter category assessments."
